We have run these previously only on Rocky Linux 9.4 (Blue Onyx), see below for the primary dependencies.
There is no required install of these, assuming you already have Python and R, as they are run
directly from the scripts. See below for required script modifications.

SLAM_HTSeq_FR_v2.py
Python (includes os and collections): 3.7.13
pandas: 1.3.5
HTSeq: 2.0.0

Before running, modify "master_dir" to the location of the testData directory
and change the path to the gtf file, such as one downlaoded from https://www.gencodegenes.org/human/

For the chr22-only test files, the run time is ~15 minutes, or 3-4 minutes per file.

For each of the directories in testDATA (i.e. cardio_DM_R1_chr22,cardio_DM_R2_chr22,cardio_dT_R1_chr22,cardio_dT_R2_chr22),
it will create a sub-directory called counts and save the following files here
  HTSeq_counts_gene.tsv
    12 column file containing gene position, strand, ID, and name. For each gene, it returns the number of reads that have
    at least one T->C conversion (TC_read_counts), total read counts for that gene (converted + unconverted), the total number of
    converted and unconverted Ts (across all reads for that gene), and the conversion rate based on the ratio of converted to
    unconverted Ts.
  HTSeq_excluded_counts_gene.tsv
    Returns the number of reads that don't align to a feature (_no_feature), ambiguous reads, and unampped


SLAM-DESeq.r
DESeq2: 1.47.3
data.table: 1.16.4
dplyr: 1.1.4
stringr: 1.5.1
comprehenr: 0.6.10

Before running, you will need to modify "hisat_out", which is really the same path as "master_dir" from SLAM_HTSeq_FR_v2.py (i.e. testData
directory), the BED_FILE path (is just a .bed file derived from the .gtf file used above, containing only genes), and the SLAM_summary_path,
which just contains basic information about the experiments so it can determine the appropriate comparisons and replicates. You can
use the example "example_SLAM_summary.txt". You can also change the nascent_filter, which I usually set to 20 for 120min 4sU labeling

For the chr22-only test files, the run time is <1 minute.

This will create a new directory in "hisat_out" called "testDESEQ-WG". This contains the DESEQ output for nascent and total
transcripts (in DMSO_deseq-analysis), nascent and total expression data and class files for GSEA (in GSEA), a "WG_merged_counts.txt" file
containing the nascent (_tc) and total (_total) counts for each gene, and nascent and total FPKM tables. Note that the output from DESEQ will
be slightly different from our findings due to the number of tests and FDR.


